=== Other ===
In March 2021, it was announced that [[Del Rey Books]] would publish ''[[Star Wars: Ronin: A Visions Novel|Ronin: A Visions Novel]]'', an original novel written by [[Emma Mieko Candon]] which builds on the story of "The Duel". It was released on October 12, 2021.<ref name="Ronin" />

An art book with creator interviews and selected production materials from all nine shorts was published by [[Dark Horse Comics]] on April 12, 2022.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Ratcliff |first=Amy |date=October 6, 2021 |title=The Art of 'Star Wars: Visions' Is Coming Next Year |url=https://nerdist.com/article/the-art-of-star-wars-visions-book-announcement-dark-horse-comics-zack-davisson/ |access-date=October 26, 2021 |website=[[Nerdist]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220105195936/https://nerdist.com/article/the-art-of-star-wars-visions-book-announcement-dark-horse-comics-zack-davisson/ |archive-date=January 5, 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref>

== ''Visions Presents'' ==
{{main|Star Wars: Visions Presents}}
At Star Wars Celebration in April 2025, the spin-off series ''[[Star Wars: Visions Presents]]'' was announced. The first of these will be ''The Ninth Jedi'', a full anime series building on the shorts of the same name. The series was released on August 5, 2026.<ref name="CinemaBlend-2025" />

